Energy required to removed electron in th $(n=2)$ stage The energy of the photon
$\begin{array}{l}
=R\left(\frac{1}{1^{2}}-\frac{1}{n^{2}}\right) \Rightarrow 13.6 \mathrm{eV}\left(\frac{1}{1}-\frac{1}{4}\right) \\
=13.6 \mathrm{eV}\left(\frac{4-1}{4}\right)=13.6 \mathrm{eV} \times \frac{3}{4}=\frac{40.8}{4} \mathrm{eV} \\
=10.2 \mathrm{eV}
\end{array}$
